/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.exe

# Node / JS
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/

# Build and analysis outputs
graphify-out/
logs/
data/
*.log

# Python bytecode: the interpreter writes `__pycache__/` and `*.pyc` as a side
# effect of running a script, so they appear mid-run and are never source.
# Default-deny them so `git add -A` cannot sweep a cache into a release commit.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets and local environment
.secrets/
.env
.env.*
cookie.txt
$resultPath

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

.opencode/

# Skill-local credentials
skills/**/*.env
skills/**/.env
**/confluence.env

# Lab scratch space: header-capture experiments write raw request material.
# Default-deny, so a new artifact extension cannot leak by accident.
# Reversible: delete this block once lab/ is curated for commit.
lab/

# Plan test evidence: per candidate screenshots, traces, console logs, and browser
# reports are generated, not authored. Default-deny the contents so `git add -A`
# cannot sweep them into a release, while keeping the folder itself so the
# evidence path in the plan always resolves. Commit a specific artifact only by
# explicit `git add -f` when a plan calls for it.
plans/evidence/**
!plans/evidence/.gitkeep

# Plan allocation database: plans/_plan.sql is the committed record, while the
# working database and its WAL siblings are rebuilt locally by plan-code.ps1 import.
plans/_plan.db*

# Agent edit backups: `<file>.bak-<timestamp>` rollback copies are local, not source.
# Default-deny so `git add -A` cannot sweep them into a release. A backup is a
# recovery aid for an untracked file edit, never a committed artifact.
*.bak-*
